WEBVTT

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.770
The wind is warm.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:35.620
<i>May. When I wake up and open the window,
I don't recoil from the wind anymore.</i>

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.750
<i>Rei Kiriyama.</i>

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.000
<i>That's my name.</i>

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.800
<i>In a small town by a big river,</i>

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.720
<i>is where I live.</i>

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:59.220
<i>Class C-1, 5th dan. Eighteen years old.</i>

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.980
<i>Profession: Pro shogi player.</i>

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.030
Setting Sun

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.780
KOMAHASHI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.450
<i>May.</i>

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.910
<i>Shogi Science Club activities
have finally begun.</i>

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.290
SCIENCE LAB

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.290
Wait, hold on.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.710
Wait a second.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.050
Eisaku Noguchi
Third-year high school student

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.550
Is it okay if I look at the book?

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.550
After School Shogi Science Club

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.800
Go ahead.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:58.800
Rei Kiriyama
Profession: Pro shogi player

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.050
Shogi
Science
Club

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.050
OOTA-KUN

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.050
Get near the king as if to surround it, eh?

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.270
MUTTER MUTTER

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.270
Former
Homeroom
Teacher

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.270
Faculty
Advisor
Takashi
Hayashida

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.770
<i>For me, this is pretty much
my first club activity.</i>

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:15.980
I could do this, but then
my bishop would be captured, so...

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.030
I... I...

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.740
I lost.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.990
SIGH

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.830
SLUMP

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:31.210
I-I didn't realize defeat
could be this painful.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.080
I-I won.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:39.050
It's because I'm never subjected to such severe
"wins" or "losses" in everyday life.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:43.930
And even worse,
I must declare the "loss" myself.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:46.430
With three pawns,
shift and slide the opponent's pieces

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.060
Even if I read the book
and come up with a strategy,

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.600
A feisty knight will be eaten by a pawn

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.690
my opponent would most likely
attack me in a different way,

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.020
The pawn under a gold general
is more solid than a rock

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.940
so I don't know what to do.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.940
Strike rooks and bishops from a distance

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:52.940
Shogi Proverb Cards by Noguchi

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:57.190
As you can see,
I even made shogi proverb cards.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:02.910
And if I come up with a plan, my opponent
will have a countermeasure to my plan,

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:07.330
forcing me to think of a countermeasure
to his countermeasures to my original plan.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.580
Bwaaa!

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.460
Ugh! There's no end to it, is there?

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.920
Well, no, there's no end to it.

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:20.050
Naturally your opponent
isn't going to go by the book,

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.010
so just be careful as you proceed.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.890
ROOK

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:29.270
First, with Climbing Silver, your goal
is to promote your rook, so please aim for that.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:34.100
As you do that, try not to
let any of your pieces be captured.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.270
And after it's promoted?

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:41.570
The ultimate goal
is to capture your opponent's king,

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.370
so you should surround that king
with as many of your pieces as possible.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.700
SILVER GENERAL

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:49.660
PROMOTED PAWN

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.540
I've got your back, Senpai!

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.620
That's reassuring.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:58.380
But if I move a lot of my pieces like that,
I'll be leaving my own castle wide open.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:53.710
BANG

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:55.460
BANG

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:57.210
BANG

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.000
BANG

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.380
You noticed that, huh? You're right.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:02.380
GROAN

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.440
Hey, hey, hey, meow!

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.190
Give us the king-meow!

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.190
Lance - Pawn - Silver General - Promoted Pawn - Bishop

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.400
You'll never...

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.650
...get our king!

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.030
Lance - Gold General - King - Gold General - Silver General

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:23.070
Because you only have
a limited number of pieces.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.530
That being said, if you only defend,
you won't be effective at attacking.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.530
DASH

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.120
This is where I prove myself!

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.200
Silver General, wait! Come back, come back!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.950
SNEAK SNEAK SNEAK

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.870
TREMBLE TREMBLE

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.870
Get away!

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:38.340
The balance between attacking and defending
is an eternal theme.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:43.130
Well, you'll just have to play a lot
so you can remember things.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:47.300
Not only from books, but these days
you can play on the internet too,

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.390
so you can enjoy playing at home
in a relaxed...

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.680
Kiriyama!

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.100
POINT

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.060
Can you beat the crap out of this guy for me?

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.390
At this rate, I'll lose!

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.400
What should my next move be?

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.560
I want to make this guy pay!

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.690
Please think on your own.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.110
What the hell? You're so cold, Kiriyama!

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:09.570
You're a stinge!

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:09.570
Stingy!

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.070
How can you do this to your old teacher?

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.570
Cheating is wrong.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.830
FLAIL

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.830
FLAIL

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:12.540
Do you allow your students to cheat on tests?

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.330
NO

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.330
NO

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.330
No, right? You understand?

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.500
I don't want to listen to reason right now!

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:20.840
It's not reason, it's the rules.
You're not a child, you know.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:27.380
Okay, let's keep playing.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.470
Don't be afraid of losing.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:32.100
If you don't play a lot,
you can't get a feel for it.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.350
Are you telling me to get used to losing?

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.270
No, don't get used to it.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.900
If you stop getting frustrated at losing,
then you'll stop studying.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:45.610
Question! How strong do I have to become
before saying farewell to this frustration?

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:52.030
Even if you get strong,
but play with someone who's better, you'll lose.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:56.290
When that happens, it's so frustrating it feels like
your innards are turning upside down.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.500
It never ends?

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:02.170
No. It's forever frustrating and forever painful.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.380
BLUNT

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.840
Except when you win.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:03.840
WHISPER

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:07.550
The stronger you get,
the more bitter defeat tastes when you lose.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.930
In fact, the more time you spend on it,
the more frustrating it gets.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:13.100
The more you progress,
the more frustrated you'll be.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.100
W-Wait a minute, Kiriyama!

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:18.440
Do you have fun when you play shogi?

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:19.690
FREEZE

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:19.690
QUIVER
QUIVER

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:21.150
F-Fun?

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.230
What?

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.950
*This background has metaphorical images as accompaniment.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:39.160
FREEZE

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:40.830
Oh no!

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.880
It's okay, Kiriyama.
H-How would you like some tea?

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.670
It's tear grass tea made with the tear grass
I acquired from the field behind the school.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:52.800
Noguchi, you really are serious about
self-sufficiency, huh?

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:55.890
I also have coffee made with dandelion roots.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.680
That's not science anymore, but agriculture.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.980
I'm going to the restroom.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:04.980
STAGGER

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:11.740
WOBBLE
WOBBLE

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:10.150
That's tear grass tea for you!
Such a pronounced diuretic effect. Hmm.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.740
Don't take too long, Kiriyama!

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:15.160
The Meijin Battle will be on TV from 4:00!

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.080
Okay, I'll be quick!

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.660
<i>That was five years ago.</i>

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:26.920
<i>If he'd boarded the train without disguising
himself, he would've been recognized.</i>

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:30.170
<i>So of course, I was fooled, too.</i>

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.880
<i>And thus 14 people...</i>

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:37.220
100 FAMOUS LAKES OF JAPAN

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:38.640
<i>The Aburasaka Pass is between
Fukui Prefecture and Gifu Prefecture.</i>

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.560
I didn't even know.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:46.560
Kiriyama is already living his life
as a professional?

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:54.320
He's already living in that harsh world
of "victories" and "defeats," huh?

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:01.250
Even the best player, Meijin Souya,
has a winning rate of 70%.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.250
He loses three out of ten matches.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:09.750
MEIJIN BATTLE
TOUJI VS KUMAKURA
SECOND MATCH

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.170
Oh, I've heard of him.

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.750
He won the "Seven Crowns," right?

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:13.760
So they're broadcasting
his match live today, huh?

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.760
Yeah. It's the second match
for the Meijin Battle.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.640
In the first match,
he lost to the challenger, Kumakura.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:25.020
The stronger you get,
the more bitter defeat tastes, huh?

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:29.270
Then when somebody at this level loses,

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:34.070
I wonder what's going on in his mind?

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.070
Oh, it's starting.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:42.040
<i>This is the first day of the second match
for the 69th Shogi Meijin Battle.</i>

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.290
Let's begin with the two players
entering the room.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.290
Challenger
Kengo Kumakura
9th-dan

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:53.010
At 8:53 am, the challenger,
Kengo Kumakura 9th-Dan, entered the room.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.550
Touji Souya
Meijin

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:01.180
And then, at 8:55 am,
Meijin Souya entered the room.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.900
The match began at 9:00 am.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.780
In just a moment,
the second match will begin.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:25.000
Souya looks like he's having fun.
I'm jealous.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.370
Well, just be patient.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.880
Souya will be coming for you
in the Kishou Tournament.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:33.130
As the challenger.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.010
Scary. But I'm looking forward to it.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:40.300
Souya has a cute face,
but he'll come to break my bones.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.060
Whew, scary, scary.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:46.770
Well, that's because the casual moves
you make mock your opponent.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:50.690
Mock? I'm always serious when I play.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:54.570
Oh, sorry. I meant,
you seriously mock your opponent.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:59.820
If I can win a slugfest,
then I'll start throwing punches.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.160
But now it's tough on me physically.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.950
After all, I'm about to hit 60.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.910
I'll probably croak in the ring.

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:12.380
When your opponent goes all out,
you don't get hurt.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:16.800
When you hit him with everything you've got,
he returns your blows at the same level.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:21.180
Souya is happy to have
an opponent like that in Kumakura.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:24.310
And vice versa, Kumakura with Soya.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:28.810
They're both thinking that their opponent

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:34.570
is a toy that won't break
no matter how hard they spin it around.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:42.240
Geez, these two make such a perfect picture.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:44.740
<i>It ran across my mind.</i>

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:48.120
<i>Right now, Mr. Shimada...</i>

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:52.130
<i>must be watching these two
from somewhere.</i>

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.840
<i>From a classroom dyed red by the setting sun,</i>

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.470
<i>the person on the screen...</i>

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:05.970
<i>...seemed to be slightly smiling.</i>

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:07.970
Setting Sun

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:11.980
Ramune

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:40.550
H-He's eating with his hands!

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:02.280
Man, he killed three pieces of cake
in mere seconds!

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.070
He gobbled them up, just like that.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.830
And his eyes were locked
on the board the whole time!

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:09.080
Such splendor.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:13.080
Still, this is an interesting scene.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.920
Right in the middle of a serious battle,
with the combatants in kimonos,

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:18.840
snacks would suddenly appear.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:22.590
And it's being broadcast across the nation.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:27.180
Well, the brain is the biggest eater
of all the organs in the body.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:30.180
And glucose is the
only nourishment it can get.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:34.480
In shogi, you need your brain
firing on all cylinders.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:38.230
And so, what is Souya...

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:00.840
He's supplementing the energy
in his brain directly!

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:02.590
How many sugar cubes was that?!

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.840
And three slices of lemon?!

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:09.470
Citric acid to recover from fatigue
and sugar for brain energy.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:11.470
It's too straightforward!
As expected from a Meijin!

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:14.890
WOW WOW
SO COOL

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:12.810
It's so efficient.

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:15.890
These two are monsters!
In more meanings that one...

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:17.350
That's what you're stuck on?

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:20.360
SHOGI HALL

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.360
Wow.

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:24.440
Three pieces of cake, wolfed down.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:27.240
Kuma has some appetite.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:31.120
He's already famous for it
on these tournament broadcasts.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:32.740
That appetite of his.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:35.160
They always show the "snack time."

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:39.880
And Kuma can put away the booze too.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.590
This is the man who ate cakes
while emptying a bottle of sweet potato shochu.

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:47.220
Does that even go together? I bet it doesn't!

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:50.600
On the other hand, we've got Souya.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:53.810
Now there's a dull man.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:56.640
You thought they were
sugar cubes, didn't you?

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.190
They aren't?

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:00.480
Pure glucose.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:05.570
What the hell?
Then he's just feeding his brain.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:07.650
How bland can you get?

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:09.160
Although that's just like him.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:17.410
I guess they sell that now, in soft cubed form.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.080
At drug stores and convenience stores.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.630
You know a lot about it.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:24.840
Souya asked me to pick some up,
when we were in Kyoto.

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.010
He said he ate what he had,
and asked me to get more.

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:31.640
Kyoto? Oh, the Lion King Tournament.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.560
With Shimada...

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:48.030
He must have used a lot of brain power
and stamina to take down Shimada.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:51.530
Although at 4-0, he made it look easy.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.540
I guess even the title-holder is desperate.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.290
69th Meijin Battle
Second Match
End

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.340
So the brain is the "biggest eater," huh?

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:10.010
Oh, Kiriyama. Do you know
what ramune is made of?

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:12.220
Huh? Uh, no.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.800
Glucose and starch.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.560
Glucose?

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:20.890
And it's easy to make.
Would you like to try making some?

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:24.060
The first day's broadcast is over anyway.

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:29.360
We should have some ingredients left over.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.150
Why do we have that?

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:34.320
We did an experimental food sampler
for last year's bazaar.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:39.830
Between natto, rice, and tear grass tea...

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.460
I swear, all you guys do is eat.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.460
It's science. All part of science.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:17:01.480
TODAY'S SCIENCE

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:08.400
Science in 20 Minutes

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:08.400
Homemade Ramune

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:16.240
First, you sift finely-crushed glucose.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.910
Then you put potato starch
and water in a beaker.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:23.500
But only that would be bland,
so let's add some citric acid.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.920
A sour flavor is refreshing in your mouth.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.920
And citric acid is also effective against fatigue.

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:28.920
LITTLE BIT

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:32.050
Then you mix it and heat it up a bit.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:35.430
That's all the citric acid you need?

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:39.010
Even a miniscule amount like this
is extremely sour.

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:43.600
After that, you mix in the glucose little by little.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:41.560
GLUCOSE

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.900
Knead it, knead it, and squeeze it!

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:49.770
And we're done!

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:49.770
BOOM

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.320
- What?
- Already?

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:55.490
Slice it into small pieces like this,

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.820
let it dry naturally, and it's ready to eat.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:06.370
It hasn't hardened yet, but go ahead.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:18.300
It really is ramune.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:22.100
Wow! So this is how ramune is made!

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:27.100
Your delightful surprise
makes the experiment worthwhile, Kiriyama.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.480
WOW

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:25.560
WOW COOL

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:27.600
WOW COOL WOW

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:29.230
HAHAHA

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:32.860
Well, shall we make some
with baking soda, too?

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:33.990
Baking soda?

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.280
Sodium bicarbonate.
It's carbonic acid.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.740
We can make it fizzy like cola.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:42.450
Can I try making some?

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:44.500
Go right ahead.

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.250
Very nice, Kiriyama.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:50.590
It seems you've come to appreciate
the wonders of science.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:52.340
This is science?

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:55.590
Of course.
What else would it be?

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:06.890
There you go.
Oh, don't put in too much water.

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:10.020
There it is. Now mix, mix...

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:13.360
Um, about this much?

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:16.950
Kiriyama, are you actually
clumsy with this stuff?

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:20.820
CITRIC ACID

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:20.070
That might be a little too much.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:21.990
- H-Huh?
- You can do it!

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:25.200
Was that too much water?

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:28.500
Kiriyama, are you a little kid?

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:32.210
Why are both of your hands
moving in the same direction?

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:37.590
I bet you can't draw a square with your right hand
while drawing a triangle with your left hand.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.180
I-I can do that!

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.260
Are you sure?

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:47.770
Don't worry, Kiriyama.
All you have to do is add more glucose.

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:49.520
- What?
- You can save it yet.

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:00.570
<i>Huh?</i>

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.030
<i>What is this?</i>

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.790
<i>I'm participating in a club activity.</i>

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.250
<i>I'm laughing and talking...</i>

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:16.550
<i>...at school.</i>

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:19.300
Now let's give it a taste test.

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:21.380
Kiriyama.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:29.930
<i>The ramune is sweet...</i>

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:36.900
<i>and when I put it in my mouth, it falls apart.</i>

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:44.660
<i>As it melted, I felt a lump in my throat.</i>

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:53.790
Kiriyama, the ones with the baking soda
are definitely the best.

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:57.210
As expected, these are more refreshing.

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:02.880
<i>If I wasn't careful, it felt like
something was going to leak from my eyes,</i>

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:05.100
<i>so I used every ounce of will to hold it in.</i>

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:11.480
Um, could I take this home?

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:20.030
<i>I wrapped the remaining ramune
in a scrap of notebook paper,</i>

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:27.620
<i>and put it in my bag.</i>

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:36.920
<i>I thought Hina and Momo would enjoy it
if I shared some with them.</i>

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.010
<i>I'll go visit them.</i>

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:44.260
<i>I'll cross that bridge...</i>

00:21:58.310 --> 00:21:59.270
<i>...and then...</i>

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:01.900
It's Rei!

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:03.490
<i>How to make ramune...</i>

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:04.570
Oh, it's Rei!

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:06.160
<i>My club activities...</i>

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:08.870
<i>About Noguchi-senpai...</i>

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:11.540
<i>About Mr. Hayashida...</i>

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:14.750
Welcome!

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:16.750
<i>I wanted to tell them...</i>

00:22:19.090 --> 00:22:20.380
<i>...all about it.</i>

00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:55.020
Oh, my.

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:08.990
It's fizzy! How is it, Momo?

00:24:10.490 --> 00:24:12.450
Rei and his friends made it.

00:24:14.830 --> 00:24:17.540
Wow! I want to try making it, too!

00:24:17.540 --> 00:24:19.330
Rei, could you teach me how?

00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:21.290
Sure, of course.

00:24:23.790 --> 00:24:25.800
Fizzy!

00:24:27.010 --> 00:24:30.010
Ramune

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:38.180
Episode 24

00:24:32.340 --> 00:24:34.680
Why! Unbelievable!

00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:38.180
This is good. That's not good.
Are you the one who decides that?

00:24:38.180 --> 00:24:40.480
Humans are the embodiment of chaos.

00:24:40.480 --> 00:24:43.520
I wouldn't want neither of them.

00:24:43.520 --> 00:24:47.730
I don't think even Souya
knows what to do.

00:24:47.730 --> 00:24:50.030
Ugh... Idiot.

00:24:51.030 --> 00:24:53.820
Please look forward to the next
"March comes in like a lion".

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:56.660
Rei, thank you!
Ramune is really delicious, huh?

00:24:56.660 --> 00:24:58.370
Fizzy!
